# The build context is sent to the Docker daemon whole, and these are 848 MB of it (measured
# 2026-10-11) that no stage of the Dockerfile uses.
#
# node_modules is deliberate, not only for the size: the builder takes its modules from the deps
# stage (`COPY --from=deps`), which installs them for Alpine, and a host copy landing on top of
# them afterwards would put another platform's native binaries in the image.
# .next is whatever was built last on the host; the builder runs `next build` itself.
# data holds the SQLite file of a running installation and belongs to that installation only.
node_modules
.next
data
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.git
*.log
